==============================================================================
NB5  DEFECT control: the planted map T1 (T1(3*2^m) = 3*2^(m+1), m >= 1; T1 = T otherwise)
==============================================================================
  on [1, 10000000]: T(n) in S1 = {3*2^m : m>=1} only if n in S1 (the 21 points of S1 below 10^7)
  [proof: T^-1(3*2^m) = {3*2^(m+1)} since 3*2^m = 0 mod 3 has no odd T-preimage].
  Hence T1-orbits from outside S1 are T-orbits (they never enter S1), S1 is one divergent T1-orbit,
  and basin_T1(1) = basin_T(1) minus S1.  Given the census above, basin_T1(1) cap [1,10^7] =
  [1,10^7] minus S1.  Its series is z/(1-z) - sum_{m>=1} z^(3*2^m) up to 2^71 (Barina), and
  irrational unconditionally (the periodicity lemma runs verbatim avoiding the density-zero S1),
  so |z| = 1 is a natural boundary.  The criterion 'B continues across an arc' is DEFECT-aware.

