  3n-1 basin of 17                                     k=2: none (full rank at every grid point); k=3: none (full rank at every grid point)
  => FINITE-EXACT: no 3n-1 basin series satisfies a 2- or 3-Mahler equation with
     (order, degree) in the grid; the solver finds the equations of every control.
  DEFECT: the planted map T1 has basin(1) = N minus {3*2^m : m>=1} (Part A, NB5); its series
  z/(1-z) - G(z), G(z) = z^6 + G(z^2), is 2-Mahler (PROVED) and irrational, while T1 has a
